Subject: Cantor Public Procedure Machine Schema Transitive Type Inventory

Description: Reproducible inventory of every named Cantor type reachable from the prepare, run, verify, and response transport roots before shared-form extraction.

@ [inventory_uuid] 74d6d4f0-585a-4faa-8c99-5d599ab739db
@ [baseline_commit] 104281548a948325b124acad2522e08a63cbb8c2
@ [rustdoc_command] RUSTC_BOOTSTRAP=1 cargo rustdoc -p cantor_core --locked --offline -- -Z unstable-options --output-format json

& [RootSet] is exact
  + CLI wrappers are ResponseStatus, CliFault, VerificationRecord, CliResponse, PrepareRequest, PreparedRunRequest, and VerifyRequest
  + core roots are SemanticId, ContentDigest, ProcedureCandidate, AuthorshipLaneTemplate, SopAnchorBinding, ProviderNeutralToolSchema, ToolCallProposal, AuthorshipLaneEvidence, and FakeControllerOutcome

& [ReachabilityMethod] is structural
  + start with each named root
  + follow every local resolved-path type through struct fields, enum variants, generic arguments, maps, sets, vectors, and options
  + include only named types owned by cantor_core plus the seven CLI-owned wrappers
  + exclude primitive, standard-library, serde, implementation, function, and trait nodes

& [ModelTypes] are 2
  + SemanticId
  + ContentDigest

& [ProcedureEnums] are 20
  + ProcedureEffectClass, ProcedureReadClass, ProcedureWriteClass, ProhibitedProcedureOperation, SchemaKind
  + ProcessOperation, ProcessLifecycle, ProcedureLifecycle, PhaseDisposition, ProcedurePhase
  + AdmissionDecision, CatalogueStatus, InvocationDisposition, ProcedureMessageKind, NegotiationStatus
  + TraceEventKind, ProcedureFaultCategory, ProcedureType, ProcedureValue, AwaitedCondition

& [ProcedureStructs] are 40
  + ProcedureBounds, SopAnchorBinding, SchemaField, TaggedVariant, ProcedureSchema, ProcedureSchemaSet
  + ProcedureEffectDeclaration, InstructionOperand, ProcessInstruction, ControlRegion, ProcessDefinition, ProcedureCandidate
  + CompiledProcedureIdentity, SourceMapEntry, CantorProcessIr, ProcessBudgetState, ProcessInstanceState
  + SerializedContinuation, ProcessStep, Participant, ProcedureMessage, NegotiatedFrame, NegotiationSession, TokenRingPass
  + ReceiptEvidence, ValidationReceipt, CompilationReceipt, VerificationReceipt, AdmissionDisposition, CatalogueReceipt
  + RevocationRecord, ProcedureCatalogueEntry, ProcedureCatalogueState, InvocationBudget, InvocationRequest
  + SemanticTraceEvent, SemanticTrace, ConsumedBudget, ProcedureFault, InvocationResult

& [AuthorshipAndCoordinationTypes] are 6
  + AuthorshipClass, AuthorshipLaneTemplate, AuthorshipLaneEvidence
  + CoordinationOutcome, CoordinationReplayReceipt, FakeObserverAdmissionPolicy

& [ToolTypes] are 11
  + ExchangeOperation, ProviderNeutralToolSchema, ToolCallProposal, ControllerEventKind, ControllerTranscriptEvent
  + ToolControllerFault, ToolResultDisposition, LaterPassContext, ProviderNeutralToolResult
  + FakeControllerTranscript, FakeControllerOutcome

& [TemporalTypes] are 1
  + SensitivityClass

& [UniqueCount] is exact
  + [core_named_type_count] is 80
  + [CLI_wrapper_type_count] is 7
  + [total_named_type_count] is 87
  + [recursive_member] is ProcedureValue through its collection and record variants

& [HonestyLimit] is explicit
  + this is a named Rust type-closure inventory, not a generated JSON Schema and not a proof that all serde behavior is expressible by JSON Schema
  + the rustdoc bootstrap flag was used only to emit read-only compiler metadata and does not become a build or release dependency
